{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Note that the series has terms that alternate in sign, has **odd** factorials in the denominator, and has **odd** powers of $~\\dfrac{1}{2}\\pi~$ in the numerator.  That suggests that we can use the Maclaurin series for $~\\sin x~$ to find the needed value.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Recall that \n\n$\\displaystyle\\sin x=x-\\frac{{{x}^{3}}}{3!}+\\frac{{{x}^{5}}}{5!}-...+{{\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\frac{{{x}^{2n+1}}}{\\left( 2n+1 \\right)!}+...$\n\nIt follows that\n\n$\\displaystyle\\sin\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)=\\frac{x}{2} -\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}{{x}^{3}}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{5}}}{5!}-...+{{\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})^{2n+1}{{x }^{2n+1}}}{\\left( 2n+1 \\right)!}+...$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Hence, the given series converges to $\\sin\\big( \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\big)$.\n\n$\\sin \\big( \\frac{\\pi}{2}  \\big)=1$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Evaluate the Maclaurin series.**\n\n$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} -\\dfrac{\\dfrac{1}{8}{{\\pi }^{3}}}{3!}+\\dfrac{{\\dfrac{1}{32}{\\pi }^{5}}}{5!}-...+{{\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{2n+1}{{\\pi }^{2n+1}}}{\\left( 2n+1 \\right)!}+...$\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$0$","correct":false},{"content":"$1$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac13$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac12$","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
